  "question": {
    "text": "The heat of combustion of solid benzoic acid at constant volume is \\(-321.30 \\mathrm{~kJ}\\) at \\(27^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}\\). The heat of combustion at constant pressure is \\((-321.30-x \\mathrm{R}) \\mathrm{kJ}\\), the value of \\(x\\) is _______.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "150",
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned} & \\mathrm{C}_6 \\mathrm{H}_5 \\mathrm{COOH}(\\mathrm{S})+\\frac{15}{2} \\mathrm{O}_2(\\mathrm{~g}) \\rightarrow 7 \\mathrm{CO}_2(\\mathrm{~g})+3 \\mathrm{H}_2 \\mathrm{O}(\\ell) \\\\ & \\Delta \\mathrm{H}=\\Delta \\mathrm{U}+\\Delta \\mathrm{n}_{\\mathrm{g}} \\mathrm{RT} \\\\ & =-321.30-\\frac{1}{2} \\frac{\\mathrm{R}}{100} \\times 300 \\\\ & =(-321.30-150 \\mathrm{R}) \\mathrm{kJ}\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
